zsh: quote a word that ends in }

zsh reads an unquoted } that ends a word as a closing brace, so the 0}
that Quote returned for "0}" with LangZsh is a parse error in zsh. bash,
ksh93 and mksh read 0} as one word, and a } inside a word is fine in zsh
too, so only a trailing } with LangZsh needs quoting.

Reproducer, before this change:

	syntax.Quote("0}", syntax.LangZsh) // 0}
	$ zsh -c 'printf %s 0}'
	zsh:1: parse error near `}'

FuzzQuote found it with zsh 5.9 on PATH; the input is a seed.

Part of https://github.com/mvdan/sh/issues/120.

diff --git a/syntax/quote.go b/syntax/quote.go
index d438dbf..896c7e9 100644
--- a/syntax/quote.go
+++ b/syntax/quote.go
@@ -86,6 +86,9 @@ func Quote(s string, lang LangVariant) (string, error) {
 		rem = rem[size:]
 		offs += size
 	}
+	if lang.in(LangZsh) && strings.HasSuffix(s, "}") {
+		shellChars = true
+	}
 	if !shellChars && !nonPrintable && !IsKeyword(s) {
 		// Nothing to quote; avoid allocating.
 		return s, nil
